//! English explanations of System › Install to disk (G1.6y), scope `install_to_disk`, sorted by key.

/// Explanations: (key, Markdown).
pub(super) const HELP: &[(&str, &str)] = &[
    ("install_to_disk.code", "## Code on the console\n\nThe disk holds something, so installing erases data. Besides its name, this needs proof that someone is at the machine: the code shows **only** on the consoles (screen and serial), with the disk and who asked. One use, 5 minutes, 3 tries, this disk only.\n\nNo screen: press the power button **3 times within 30 seconds** while the request is open. Otherwise the button powers off, as always.\n\nNot you? Do nothing: the code expires and nothing is erased."),
    ("install_to_disk.col_bus", "## Bus\n\nHow the disk is attached: SATA, NVMe, USB, virtio. A USB stick usually is not where a router should live."),
    ("install_to_disk.col_holds", "## Holds\n\nWhat was found on the disk, which decides the confirmation. **empty**: only the name. **data** or **CoreRouter**: the name and a code shown on the console."),
    ("install_to_disk.col_model", "## Model\n\nThe model the disk reports. Virtual disks often report none."),
    ("install_to_disk.col_name", "## Name\n\nThe kernel's name for the disk. It is what you type to confirm, so compare it, the size and the serial with the disk you mean."),
    ("install_to_disk.col_size", "## Size\n\nThe capacity of the disk. The image needs less than 1 GiB; the rest of the disk becomes the configuration partition."),
    ("install_to_disk.confirm", "## Confirmation\n\nWhat it asks depends on the disk:\n\n- **empty**: its name, typed;\n- **data**: the name and the console's code;\n- **CoreRouter**: the name and the console's code, with the option to keep its configuration.\n\nEmpty means zero in the first and last MiB and in 64 samples across the disk. Data only between the samples goes unnoticed: check size and serial.\n\nBefore writing, the router looks at the disk again. If it changed, nothing is written."),
    ("install_to_disk.disks", "## Disks\n\nThe disks of this machine and what each holds. The installation medium, a read-only disk, a disk smaller than the image or one in use by RAID or LVM are not offered: hover the chip for why.\n\nA stick plugged in now shows up by itself. **Rescan** looks at the contents again."),
    ("install_to_disk.keep", "## Keep configuration\n\nInstalls the image and keeps the `/config` of the CoreRouter on the disk: users, passwords, addresses, port names and certificate. The management port and password of this window do not apply: what is there does."),
    ("install_to_disk.mgmt", "## Management after install\n\nHow the installed router will be reached. The suggestion is the port this GUI came through.\n\n**Keep DHCP** runs a DHCP client on that port: the server tends to keep the address but does not promise it (RFC 2131 §4.3.1), so it may change and the GUI may not find the router after the reboot; the console shows the new one.\n\n**Fix current address** saves the address, gateway and DNS that DHCP gave now. Careful: if the server keeps handing that address out, there is a conflict; reserve it on the server or take it out of the range.\n\n**None**: the console offers the setup on the first boot."),
    ("install_to_disk.network", "## Network test\n\nWhat can be known before erasing a disk: driver, link and speed of each port, address, whether the gateway answers (ARP) and whether DNS answers.\n\nIt only warns: you can install anyway, for example on a network that does not exist yet.\n\n**Firmware:** the live image has no firmware files. A card that needs them may run in a reduced mode here and in full once installed.\n\n**A port without a driver** does not show up here at all: it may not exist for the live image. Use the console then."),
    ("install_to_disk.overview", "## Install to disk\n\nThis machine runs the image from the installation medium, in RAM: the disk was not touched and nothing survives a reboot. Routing, firewall, NAT and servers are off here; only what tests the network and installs works.\n\nChoose the disk, check the network and the management port, and install. The image is checked by its signature and read back from the disk once written. Leave the medium in the machine until the end.\n\nThe console stays an alternative: **i** and Enter opens the text installer."),
    ("install_to_disk.password", "## Admin password\n\nThe password of the installed router. It also applies now, on this live image. The disk gets only the hash.\n\nBlank: the installed router has no password, takes the empty password from any network and warns until one is set."),
    ("menu.install_to_disk", "## What it does\nInstalls on a disk the image running from the installation medium (ISO). Only on the live image; on an installed router, update through **Packages**."),
];
